# startup.xpl.template -- a documented starting point for your own startup.xpl.
#
# Copy this file to `startup.xpl` (next to the XyScript program) and uncomment the
# lines you want. XyScript runs `startup.xpl` automatically at launch, from the
# folder the program itself lives in ($XSDIR). Because the working directory starts
# at $XSDIR, the plain relative paths below resolve against THAT folder -- so you can
# zip the whole folder, move it to another machine, unzip it, and everything still
# loads, the same on Windows, macOS, and Linux.
#
# Lines beginning with '#' are ignored.

# --- Shelling to the operating system -------------------------------------
# TRUST 0 blocks the `X`/shell verbs; TRUST 1 allows them:
# trust 0

# --- Keyboard map ---------------------------------------------------------
# Load your key bindings from a .kbd file sitting beside this one:
# loadkbd mykeys.kbd

# --- Configuration & colour theme -----------------------------------------
# Load saved settings (colours, toggles), then apply a theme preset or your own:
# loadcfg mysettings.cfg
# theme themes/foolscap.xpl

# --- Auto-replace & libraries ---------------------------------------------
# loadar mypairs.ar
# loadlib mylib.lib

# --- Where to start editing ----------------------------------------------
# You start in the program folder. To begin in your documents instead,
# uncomment and set a path (absolute, or ~ for your home folder):
# cd ~/Documents
